    <string name="settings_rotate_id">Rotate advertised ID</string>
    <string name="settings_rotate_id_help">Advertise a new ID at the start of every client period. Stock clients exchange at most once per ID until the server data changes, so this lets each nearby client exchange once per period.</string>
    <string name="settings_keep_awake">Keep awake</string>
    <string name="settings_start_on_boot">Start automatically</string>
    <string name="settings_start_on_boot_help">Start relaying after the phone restarts or the app is updated, without opening the app (not after you press Stop). With a PIN or pattern lock, unlock once after a restart.</string>
    <string name="settings_keep_awake_help">Recommended for a plugged-in relay. Holds a partial wake lock while the dropbox is cycling (not paused or stopped). Without it, Android suspends the CPU with the screen off, the role timers stop counting, and the dropbox can stay in one role far longer than its period.</string>
    <string name="settings_reset_defaults">Reset all to defaults</string>
    <string name="settings_server_keys">Server keys (QR)</string>
    <string name="settings_server_keys_help">The DDD server whose keys the dropbox trusts. It accepts only recency blobs signed by this server and sends its storage reports to it. To use another server (for example a laptop server), scan the QR code from its /qr page, or paste the https://discdd.net/srvr?… URL. Changing keys gives the dropbox a new client identity at that server.</string>
